  "description": "A deterministic representative 256-colour palette (16 hues x 16 luminances) for the GTIA video chip used in the Atari 400/800/XL/XE family, generated from a documented YUV colour-wheel decode rather than captured from any single emulator or real unit. No single canonical GTIA RGB table exists: real output depends on the NTSC/PAL/SECAM video standard (SECAM units expose only 8 luminances, i.e. 128 usable combinations), the analog encoder revision, and the attached display.",
